#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:4
msgid "Build a Python C/C++ extension using Conan and conan-py-build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:6
msgid ""
"In this example, we are going to create a small Python package with a C++ "
"extension that uses `pybind11 <https://pybind11.readthedocs.io/>`_ to expose "
"the C++ code to Python and `fmt <https://fmt.dev/>`_ as a regular C++ "
"dependency. Both dependencies are downloaded and built by Conan, driven by "
"`conan-py-build <https://github.com/conan-io/conan-py-build>`_, a `PEP 517 "
"<https://peps.python.org/pep-0517/>`_ build backend that lets ``pip`` (or "
"``build``, or ``uv``) build the C/C++ part of a Python package through Conan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:14
msgid ""
"Please, first clone the sources to recreate this project. You can find them "
"in the `examples2 repository <https://github.com/conan-io/examples2>`_ in "
"GitHub:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:17
msgid ""
"$ git clone https://github.com/conan-io/examples2.git\n"
"$ cd examples2/examples/extensions/python_build_backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:22
msgid "The project has this structure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:24
msgid ""
".\n"
"├── pyproject.toml\n"
"├── conanfile.py\n"
"├── CMakeLists.txt\n"
"├── LICENSE\n"
"├── src\n"
"│   └── myadder.cpp\n"
"└── python\n"
"    └── myadder\n"
"        └── __init__.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:37
msgid "Let's have a look at the *pyproject.toml* file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:39
msgid "**pyproject.toml**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:39
msgid ""
"[build-system]\n"
"requires = [\"conan-py-build\"]\n"
"build-backend = \"conan_py_build.build\"\n"
"\n"
"[project]\n"
"name = \"myadder\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"description = \"A simple Python package with a C++ extension\"\n"
"license = \"MIT\"\n"
"license-files = [\"LICENSE\"]\n"
"requires-python = \">=3.8\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.conan-py-build.wheel]\n"
"packages = [\"python/myadder\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:57
msgid ""
"Setting ``conan-py-build`` as the ``build-backend`` means that every time "
"this package is built (``pip wheel .``, ``pip install .``, ``python -m "
"build``, etc.), the backend will read the recipe declared in the standard "
"*conanfile.py*, resolve and install its dependencies through Conan, run the "
"``build()`` and ``package()`` methods, and copy everything ``package()`` "
"staged into the resulting wheel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:63
msgid ""
"The ``[tool.conan-py-build.wheel]`` section tells the backend where the pure "
"Python part of the package lives, so it also gets copied into the wheel next "
"to the compiled extension. See the `configuration reference <https://conan-"
"py-build.conan.io/configuration/>`_ for all the available options (dynamic "
"versioning, extra Conan profiles/arguments, entry points, sdist contents, "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:69
msgid ""
"Now, the *conanfile.py* is a regular Conan recipe, no different from one "
"used to create a C++ package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:72
msgid "**conanfile.py**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:72
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.tools.cmake import CMake, cmake_layout\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class MyAdderConan(ConanFile):\n"
"    name = \"myadder\"\n"
"    settings = \"os\", \"compiler\", \"build_type\", \"arch\"\n"
"    generators = \"CMakeToolchain\", \"CMakeDeps\"\n"
"\n"
"    def layout(self):\n"
"        cmake_layout(self)\n"
"\n"
"    def requirements(self):\n"
"        self.requires(\"pybind11/3.0.1\")\n"
"        self.requires(\"fmt/12.1.0\")\n"
"\n"
"    def build(self):\n"
"        cmake = CMake(self)\n"
"        cmake.configure()\n"
"        cmake.build()\n"
"\n"
"    def package(self):\n"
"        cmake = CMake(self)\n"
"        cmake.install()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:100
msgid ""
"It declares **pybind11** and **fmt** as regular requirements, downloaded as "
"precompiled binaries from ConanCenter (or built from source if needed), and "
"uses :ref:`CMakeToolchain<conan_tools_cmaketoolchain>` and :ref:"
"`CMakeDeps<conan_tools_cmakedeps>` to configure and build the extension with "
"CMake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:107
msgid ""
"``conan-py-build`` automatically points ``CMakeToolchain`` at the same "
"Python interpreter driving the build (``Python3_EXECUTABLE``/"
"``Python_EXECUTABLE``), so the recipe doesn't need to set it and CMake can't "
"pick up a different, ABI-incompatible Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:114
msgid ""
"For the compiled extension to be importable, it must land under a directory "
"that matches the Python package name, so the ``.so``/``.pyd`` ends up next "
"to ``__init__.py`` in the wheel. This is controlled by the ``DESTINATION`` "
"argument of CMake's ``install(TARGETS ...)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:119
msgid ""
"The *CMakeLists.txt* builds the ``_core`` extension module with pybind11, "
"links it against ``fmt``, and installs it into a ``myadder`` folder to match "
"the Python package name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:123
msgid "**CMakeLists.txt**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:123
msgid ""
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.15)\n"
"project(myadder LANGUAGES CXX)\n"
"\n"
"find_package(Python3 REQUIRED COMPONENTS Interpreter Development.Module)\n"
"set(PYBIND11_FINDPYTHON ON)\n"
"find_package(pybind11 CONFIG REQUIRED)\n"
"find_package(fmt REQUIRED)\n"
"\n"
"pybind11_add_module(_core src/myadder.cpp)\n"
"target_link_libraries(_core PRIVATE pybind11::module fmt::fmt)\n"
"\n"
"install(TARGETS _core DESTINATION myadder)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:139
msgid ""
"The C++ source exposes an ``add()`` function to Python, using **fmt** to "
"print the result in bold green text:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:142
msgid "**src/myadder.cpp**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:142
msgid ""
"#include <pybind11/pybind11.h>\n"
"#include <fmt/core.h>\n"
"#include <fmt/color.h>\n"
"\n"
"namespace py = pybind11;\n"
"\n"
"double add(double a, double b) {\n"
"    double result = a + b;\n"
"    fmt::print(fg(fmt::color::green) | fmt::emphasis::bold,\n"
"               \"{} + {} = {}\\n\", a, b, result);\n"
"    return result;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"PYBIND11_MODULE(_core, m) {\n"
"    m.doc() = \"Simple Python extension using fmt via Conan.\";\n"
"    m.def(\"add\", &add, \"Add two numbers and print the result formatted "
"with fmt.\",\n"
"          py::arg(\"a\"), py::arg(\"b\"));\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:164
msgid ""
"And finally, *python/myadder/__init__.py* just re-exports the function from "
"the compiled module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:167
msgid "**python/myadder/__init__.py**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:167
msgid ""
"from myadder._core import add\n"
"\n"
"__all__ = [\"add\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:175
msgid "Build and test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:177
msgid ""
"Build the wheel with ``pip``. There's no need to install ``conan-py-build`` "
"beforehand: since it's declared under ``[build-system] requires`` in "
"*pyproject.toml*, ``pip`` installs it (and Conan itself) into an isolated "
"build environment automatically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:182
msgid "$ pip wheel . -w dist/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:186
msgid ""
"Conan will install **pybind11** and **fmt**, build the extension with CMake, "
"and ``conan-py-build`` will assemble the resulting wheel and save it into "
"the *dist* folder, e.g. *dist/myadder-0.1.0-cp312-cp312-macosx_14_0_arm64."
"whl* (the exact filename depends on your platform and Python version)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:191
msgid ""
"A wheel is just a zip file, so you can check what got packaged without "
"installing it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:194
msgid ""
"$ python -m zipfile -l dist/myadder-*.whl\n"
"File Name                                             Modified             "
"Size\n"
"myadder/__init__.py                            2026-07-08 14:01:30           "
"49\n"
"myadder/_core.cpython-312-darwin.so            2026-07-08 14:41:12       "
"233288\n"
"myadder-0.1.0.dist-info/METADATA               2026-07-08 14:41:08          "
"212\n"
"myadder-0.1.0.dist-info/WHEEL                  2026-07-08 14:41:12          "
"101\n"
"myadder-0.1.0.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE       2026-07-08 14:01:32         "
"1083\n"
"myadder-0.1.0.dist-info/RECORD                 2026-07-08 14:41:12          "
"471"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:205
msgid ""
"Note how the compiled ``_core`` extension, the one Conan's ``package()`` "
"staged during the build, ends up right next to ``__init__.py`` under "
"``myadder/`` — exactly the layout the ``DESTINATION`` in *CMakeLists.txt* "
"was set up for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:209
msgid "Now install it and try it out:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:211
msgid ""
"$ pip install dist/myadder-*.whl\n"
"$ python -c \"from myadder import add; add(2, 3)\"\n"
"2 + 3 = 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/python/build_backend/build_python_extension_with_conan.rst:217
msgid ""
"The line above is printed by the C++ extension in bold green, courtesy of "
"**fmt** — a visible sign that the compiled code, not Python, produced it."
msgstr ""

